# TODO Authoring (Repo Convention)

This repo’s work units are sequential `TODO_XX.md` files.

## Location (required)

- **All TODO files MUST live in** `docs/TODOS/`.
- The filename format is **exactly** `TODO_XX.md` (two-digit, zero-padded), e.g. `TODO_01.md`.
- Do **not** create `TODO_*.md` at the repo root or anywhere else (the only allowed location is `docs/TODOS/`).

## Sequencing (required)

- When creating a new TODO, pick the **next available number** after the highest existing `TODO_XX.md` in `docs/TODOS/`.
- Keep TODOs **small and atomic** (a single coherent deliverable).
- Use `Status: TODO | IN_PROGRESS | DONE` (only these values).

## Content (required template)

Use the canonical sections below (copy/paste):

```md
# TODO_XX: <short title>

Status: TODO

## Context

- Links: <PRD.md / SYSTEM_DESIGN.md / SECURITY.md as needed>

## Description

<What to implement/change and why.>

## Expected Inputs

- <Input 1>
- <Input 2>

## Expected Outputs

- <Output 1>
- <Output 2>

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] <Criterion 1>
- [ ] <Criterion 2>

## Test Plan

- <Which tests to write >

## Files (expected)

- <Paths you expect to touch (optional)>

## Notes / Non-goals

- <Anything explicitly out of scope>
```

## Closing a TODO (required)

- Before marking `Status: DONE`:
  - Ensure `yarn test` passes.
  - Ensure no new TypeScript errors are introduced.
- Add a short note under the status line (or in a “Notes” subsection) describing what changed.
